decision: changes-requested

Two medium blockers remain:

- **N1 — successful retries are discarded**, [kept_cache.go:37](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2289309520/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/kept_cache.go:37). After the first computation fails, waiting callers recompute outside cache coordination. Their successful results are never retained, so concurrent recovery duplicates work and later callers recompute again.
- **N2 — eviction removes in-flight coordination**, [kept_cache.go:41](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2289309520/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/kept_cache.go:41). Reaching capacity clears pending entries too. Another caller can then compute a key whose original computation is still running, violating R6.

R1-F1 through R1-F3 are fixed. R1-F4 is partially fixed.

Targeted cache tests, their race run, and shallow-checkout tests passed. Additional probes could not compile because the sandbox refused a new Go build directory; the findings above rest on source inspection. The worktree remains unchanged.

Rules applied: bugfix review workflow; backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Full validation conclusions below use the supplied sealed evidence. The reported performance measurement was not independently repeated.

